#
# The vendored goldens are held byte for byte: SHA256SUMS, and the git-object chain from PIN to
# every file's blob (tests/common/spec_goldens.rs). So git never converts a line ending in them,
# on any checkout (a Windows `core.autocrlf=true` would rewrite every LF file, and the sums and
# blob ids with it) — and testdata/games/link/digest/crlf.toml holds CRLF on purpose: the link
# digest reads it as LF (manifest.md §2.6.1; AstraPlugins' own `.gitattributes` says `-text` for
# it too). Here, beside astraplugins/ and not in it, because the vendor script replaces that
# folder whole.
astraplugins/** -text
